abstract: |-
  ARCH (Adaptive Reactive CUDA Hydrodynamics) is a C++20 and CUDA simulation code for finite-volume compressible hydrodynamics, heat transfer and nuclear reactions with adaptive mesh refinement. CPU and CUDA backends share physical and numerical formulations. The optional ARCH Studio provides parameter editing, configuration and builds, initial-field and AMR previews, run and restart control, and read-only Plotfile inspection.

  Version 1.4.1 simplifies Linux and native Windows dependency preparation and builds through shared Core and desktop profiles. Illustrated Studio guides explain model and parameter selection, Preview, Run and Plotfile inspection. The documentation separates build configuration from application usage and removes obsolete plans and intermediate development records.

  cuDSS remains optional for ordinary CUDA and DenseLU calculations. Core and Studio share execution preflight checks that resolve the requested backend and solver before mesh construction. Required sparse dependencies are checked before Run, Windows launch environments check linked runtime DLLs, and strict GPU sparse qualification requires actual tests. Mathematical implementations, memory pools, scientific file readers and writers, and numerical thresholds are unchanged.

  Linux remains recommended. Native Windows provides the corresponding CPU/CUDA and Studio workflows within the documented platform and scientific scope, with newer support that may still have instability or bugs. The software release date is 2026-11-02. GitHub provides the versioned source release; no v1.4.1 Zenodo record or version-specific DOI has been published. The citation DOI identifies the existing version series.

  AI-assisted tools contributed to implementation, documentation and code review. Human contributors designed the overall software architecture and retain responsibility for scientific definitions, numerical acceptance, code review and release decisions.
